  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BAHAMAS SBIRD CONS INIT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Bahamas contains thousands of acres of pristine intertidal habitat critical for the survival of thirty- two documented neotropical shorebird species, including an estimated fifty percent of the Atlantic population of the threatened piping plover. This project will educate the Bahamian government, conservation NGOs and key stakeholders about the importance of the Bahamas for priority shorebirds, and to advocate for their inclusion of two critical sites in the governments conservation commitments. Benefitted species include short-billed dowitcher, black-bellied plover, Wilsons plover, red knot, reddish egret, and American oystercatcher...</narrative>
  </description>
